            <ArticleTitle>Rehospitalizations: packaging discharge and transition services to prevent &quot;bounce backs&quot;.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>8-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There are many factors that can reduce the rates of rehospitalization, including transition or discharge coaches who work with the patient before, during, and after the discharge; better collaboration between hospitals and physicians to improve promptness and reliability of follow-up care; and earlier medical follow-up after surgical procedures.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
